by the signing orchestrator; nested agents belong to their parent's receipt.\n\nAgent mode may expose internal owners and commands, but must still be concise enough to operate and must never dump secrets, cookies, tokens, private logs, raw provider payloads, or unnecessary bulk output. A downstream skill emits this detail only when the caller explicitly requested agent mode.\n\nWhen the receiving agent will run in a new operator-started conversation, apply the conversation-continuity contract already selected by the reporting owner. Apply its stabilization gate and emit its copyable restart prompt; never imply that Codex created, closed, or restarted the conversation itself.\n\n</instruction>","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"resource_id\":\"router\",\"spans\":null}","call_id":"A1-model-015","id":"fc_model-015","name":"instruction_read","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-015","id":"fco_01a11cec-fc60-7843-afea-76a560fe6d43","output":"<instruction>\n---\nname: 000-shipglows\ndescription: \"Execute clear bounded requests directly and route unknown, unbounded, or directional work.\"\nargument-hint: <instruction>\n---\n\nPrimary artifact type: `entrypoint-router`.\n\n## Canonical Paths\n\nBefore resolving owned paths, load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/canonical-paths.md`.\nShared references: `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/`;\nnever substitute project shadows or memory.\n\n## Intent-to-Outcome Ownership\n\nNon-trivial routing loads `intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`; resolve\n`project -> business/brand/product -> outcome -> surface -> work item` from evidence\nunder one public owner here. If sufficiency, authority, freshness, conflict,\ncompaction or handoff may change routing, load `context-quality-contract.md`;\nkeep its qualified Context Capsule, never memory as truth.\n\nOffer once to privately remember verified reusable pointers to avoid future research, unless known saved or declined. Do not inspect private stores or presume\nabsence; route to `sg-private` only after interest.\n\n## Chantier Tracking\n\nTrace category: `non-applicable`. Process role: `helper`.\nOwner alone writes specs, bug/release scopes, Skill Run History, deployments\nand lifecycle state. `(local)` if needed; bounded execution is excepted, never a chantier.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nFor final reports load `reporting-contract.md`: concise active-language\n`report=user`, even if blocked; agent detail needs explicit request.\nContinue safely runnable authorized work instead of a command.\n\n## Explicit Invocation Preflight\n\nExplicit invocations (including `$shipglows`) load `skill-invocation-preflight.md`\nand run its checker: valid silent; invalid/ambiguous activates no substitute.\nFirst-token expert aliases load `expert-mode-aliases.md` before natural routing:\npublic owner -> owner mode -> internal engine. Numeric legacy commands use\n`skill-code-index.md`. Never pass aliases to shells.\n\n## Bounded Direct-Execution Gate\n\nBefore loading routing, topology, or owner-skill references, keep clear bounded\nrequests in direct main-thread execution: few enumerable actions/targets, discoverable\nby focused lookup, no material direction to select, and focused proof sufficient.\nThis includes exact edits, exact-scope commits, ordinary resolved pushes or a small\nsequence; local/remote and model reasoning do not change classification. It does not authorize a chantier.\n\nBefore any direct or routed mutation, load `mutation-plan-approval.md`. Apply its\nrequest-derived or standing authority; otherwise use 🧭 VALIDATION RAPIDE for a\nbounded agent proposal and 🧭 PLAN À VALIDER for unbounded/directional work.\nMaterial expansion pauses. Preserve unrelated dirty work and all dedicated safety gates.\n\nDo not load a domain or lifecycle skill: direct work needs no owner skill.\nAn explicitly named skill still activates in its smallest safe mode;\nlet that skill reroute explicitly.\n`skill-execution-fidelity.md` is advisory here; apply the gate above and smallest relevant proof.\n\n### Bounded internal reference-register updates\n\nA supplied-link update qualifies when one focused local lookup suffices, public\nURLs/category are supplied, `candidate` is the only added status, no interpretation\nor public claim is needed, and duplicate/row proof suffices. Use original authority,\nappend factually without launching source intake, market study, or documentation topology work;\notherwise normal routing/approval applies. Use one primary-source check per supplied reference.\n`veille <URL>` analyzes without persistence; `concurrent <URL>` or `inspiration <URL>`\nupdates its register. `veille` takes precedence.\n\n## Delegation And Topology\n\nDirect handoff needs no delegation procedure. Never launch the selected master as\na nested subagent; the owner controls topology. Load `master-delegation-semantics.md`\nbefore actual delegation. A routing scout must pass that gate, stays read-only,\ncannot invoke skills, mutate or delegate, and returns only a route recommendation.\n\n## Shared Routing Reference\n\nLoad `decision-quality-contract.md` before non-trivial outcome selection.\nKnown ShipGlows skill/doctrine audit -> `900-shipglows-core audit`; known skill\nchange -> `900-shipglows-core build`. Only unresolved owner/mode loads\n`entrypoint-routing.md`. Do not load the matrix after a route is resolved.\nPure help needs no outcome execution, matrix, delegation or procedural pack.\nNamed profiles load `profile-activation.md` and minimal profile context; focus tags\nload `shipglows-terms.md` and matching explicit gates; source intake loads\n`source-intake-classification.md`. Sparse/partnership decisions load\n`operator-partnership-contract.md` through the intention core.\n\nURL/browser/MCP/app/connector/runtime-dependent work loads `agent-runtime-awareness.md`:\nread the global environment, managed project ENVIRONMENT and matching live registry.\nCurrent-turn direct/deferred tools determine callability, not recorded installation.\nNever start a replacement server or guess a default URL.\n\n## Mission\n\nShipGlows maintenance targets `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT`, not the current application unless explicitly\nspecified otherwise. `core` binds every remaining word to the system, including\nquoted application evidence; never redirect part of it to that application.\n\n## Mode Detection\n\nParse `$ARGUMENTS`. Empty/help answers directly; full help may use `302-sg-help`.\nAn explicitly named skill remains authoritative. Natural language applies the\nbounded gate first, then selection. Explicit maintainer workstation, editable full\nclone or \"version dev de ShipGlows\" preserves installation ownership; generic\n`full`, `all`, environment or corpus never implies a maintainer channel switch.\n\nBefore selection extract `#local`, `#nolocal`, `#ci` wherever present and load\n`execution-posture-tags.md`; reject conflicts. Preserve ordinary focus tags and\nowner authority; `#ci` implies nolocal and deferred proof, never external-write authority.\n\nFor `update`, `context`/`contexte`/`env`/`environment`, `auto`, or legacy `nolocal`, load\n`$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/entrypoint-special-modes.md`. Apply only the selected mode.\nContext is read-only; update resolves channel first. Explicit Auto implies nolocal,\nfreezes the current project, rejects local, and never means `300-sg-docs auto`.\nLegacy nolocal requires an objective, loads `no-local-execution-policy.md`, normalizes\nto `<objective> #nolocal`, and preserves ordinary ownership/approval. Bare nolocal\nnever invokes Auto or selects work.\n\n`git` -> `sg-engineering github` (read-only default); `hygiene` -> current-project\n`sg-maintenance hygiene` read-only audit; `hygiene git` -> `sg-engineering github clean`.\nReject workspace/multi-project hygiene. `verify` preserves design/accessibility/UI,\nSEO, release/live or bug specialist ownership, otherwise `sg-engineering verify`.\nGeneric verification never replaces a specialist audit.\nKnown helpers: context priming -> `301-sg-context`; cross-project state ->\n`308-sg-status`; paused work -> `706-continue`. Alias tables own remaining mappings.\n\n## Handoff And Question Contract\n\nPass original instruction, arguments, scope, authority, active language and explicit\nreport mode to one owner and continue. Preserve onboarding/first-success intent\nthrough `sg-development`. Before routing questions load `question-contract.md`;\nask one numbered question only for material operator-owned truth changing route or\nsafety, never discoverable paths. Never stop at a command recommendation for runnable work.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nStop for missing contracts, unresolved material product/data/security/permission/\ndeployment/ship decisions, nested master execution, unapproved destructive/production/\npayment/auth/tenant/secret/dirty-file scope, or bypassed evidence, verification,\nclosure or ship gates. Material expansion never inherits silent authorization.\n\n## Final Report\n\nApply the report contract; show routing only when useful. A valid route is not completion proof.\n\n</instruction>","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"resource_id\":\"router-public\",\"spans\":null}","call_id":"A1-model-016","id":"fc_model-016","name":"instruction_read","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-016","id":"fco_01a11cec-fd52-7730-9a4c-b9f855a763b0","output":"<instruction>\n---\nname: shipglows\ndescription: Route ShipGlows requests to the right métier owner.\n---\n\n# ShipGlows\n\n## Mission\n\nCanonical public router. Preserve `project -> business/brand/product -> outcome\n-> surface -> work item`, the named specialist and authority through the handoff.\n\n## Scope Gate\n\nThe engine selects the smallest safe route and continues in this conversation.\n\n## Required References\n\nResolve `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT` from the process. On Windows, if empty, read its\ncurrent-user environment value, then `%USERPROFILE%\\.shipglows\\development-channel.json`.\nA valid absolute `channel: linked` root containing `skills/000-shipglows/SKILL.md`\nwins before the installed default `$HOME/.shipglows/runtime`. Verify root and\nengine, then load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/000-shipglows/SKILL.md`.\nIf missing or invalid, stop visibly; never substitute a sibling or guessed checkout.\n\nThe engine owns conditional loaders; do not preload alias tables, domain skills\nor every reference here. For non-trivial outcomes it loads\n`$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`.\n\n## Validation\n\nKeep one owner, proof and authority limits. Clear bounded requests do not authorize\na chantier. Material uncertainty or scope growth stops for an operator-owned decision.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nStop for missing canonical contracts or unresolved authority; never guess a fallback.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nLoad `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before reporting.\nDefault to concise active-language output; agent detail requires explicit request.\nContinue safely agent-runnable authorized work before returning control.\n\n</instruction>","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"resource_id\":\"tracking\",\"spans\":null}","call_id":"A1-model-017","id":"fc_model-017","name":"instruction_read","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-017","id":"fco_01a11cec-fe39-7e22-ad72-04364d404a33","output":"<instruction>\n---\nartifact: technical_guidelines\nmetadata_schema_version: \"1.0\"\nartifact_version: \"0.10.0\"\nproject: ShipGlows\ncreated: \"2026-04-27\"\nupdated: \"2026-08-27\"\nstatus: draft\nsource_skill: 102-sg-start\nscope: chantier-tracking\nowner: Diane\nconfidence: high\nrisk_level: medium\nsecurity_impact: none\ndocs_impact: yes\nlinked_systems:\n  - shipglows_data/workflow/specs/\n  - skills/*/SKILL.md\n  - skills/000-shipglows/SKILL.md\n  - skills/004-sg-deploy/SKILL.md\n  - skills/002-sg-maintain/SKILL.md\n  - skills/006-sg-design/SKILL.md\n  - skills/references/reporting-contract.md\n  - skills/references/final-report-timestamp.md\n  - skills/references/master-workflow-lifecycle.md\ndepends_on:\n  - artifact: \"shipglows_data/workflow/specs/specs-as-chantier-registry.md\"\n    artifact_version: \"1.0.0\"\n    required_status: \"ready\"\nsupersedes: []\nevidence:\n  - \"Spec specs-as-chantier-registry.md defines shipglows_data/workflow/specs/ as the global chantier registry.\"\n  - \"shipglows added as the primary helper router; selected owner skills own durable state and chantier tracing.\"\n  - \"004-sg-deploy added as a lifecycle release orchestrator.\"\n  - \"002-sg-maintain promoted from recurring maintenance source-de-chantier to lifecycle master skill.\"\n  - \"Compact user-facing reporting contract added with explicit agent handoff mode.\"\n  - \"Master workflow lifecycle reference added: bug work items use shipglows_data/workflow/bugs/*.md as source of truth; shipglows_data/workflow/BUGS.md is optional/generated/triage view.\"\n  - \"Final report timestamp moved into a shared reporting brick loaded through reporting-contract.md.\"\n  - \"006-sg-design added as an obligatoire lifecycle master skill.\"\n  - \"003-sg-bug clarified as bug lifecycle execution through owner skills and bounded subagents.\"\n  - \"900-shipglows-core consolidated as the lifecycle core audit and packaging owner.\"\n  - \"User decision 2026-07-16: replace the trailing user-mode chantier block with a local/spec chantier name header before the verdict.\"\n  - \"User decision 2026-07-16: the verdict header displays Paris time only, without the date.\"\n  - \"User decision 2026-07-16: normal chantier headers use 🧱 and 🚧 is reserved for genuinely blocked runs.\"\n  - \"Operator correction 2026-07-18: chantier-potential reporting must not make operators launch or interpret internal workflow commands.\"\n  - \"2026-08-03 pilotage consolidation moved tasks, backlog, priorities, review, and Codex-session management under 011-sg-pilotage while preserving the pilotage process role.\"\nnext_review: \"2026-05-27\"\nnext_step: \"/103-sg-verify Specs as chantier registry\"\n---\n\n# Chantier Tracking Doctrine\n\n`shipglows_data/workflow/specs/` is the global registry for spec-first chantiers. Do not create a separate registry in `TASKS.md`, `AUDIT_LOG.md`, `PROJECTS.md` (legacy/compat only), or root `specs/`.\n\n## Two-Axis Classification\n\nChantier tracking has two separate axes. Do not collapse them into one label.\n\nTrace category answers: may this skill write a run trace into an existing chantier spec?\n\n- `obligatoire`: lifecycle spec-first skills. When a unique chantier spec is identified, read the spec, append or update `Skill Run History`, update `Current Chantier Flow`, and open the user report with the `(spec)` chantier header from `skills/references/reporting-contract.md`.\n- `conditionnel`: cross-cutting skills. Trace only when the run is attached to one unique chantier spec. If no unique spec is available, do not write to any spec and use a `(local)` chantier header. Final output still follows `skills/references/reporting-contract.md`.\n- `non-applicable`: helper/session/discovery skills. Do not write to specs and use a `(local)` chantier header for the current goal. Non-applicable for spec trace does not forbid non-spec durable artifacts when a skill contract allows them (for example `700-sg-explore` and `exploration_report`).\n\nProcess role answers: can this skill originate, support, steer, or merely inspect a chantier?\n\n- `lifecycle`: creates, readies, executes, verifies, closes, or ships a unique chantier.\n- `source-de-chantier`: may reveal work that deserves a new spec when no unique chantier exists.\n- `support-de-chantier`: helps execute or document a chantier but should not normally originate one.\n- `pilotage`: manages priorities, backlog, tasks, review, or continuation; can route to `100-sg-spec` on explicit user intent, but does not turn every planning note into a chantier.\n- `helper`: read-only or session helper; does not propose a chantier unless the user explicitly asks to formalize one.\n\n`source-de-chantier` is not a trace category. A skill can be `conditionnel` for spec writes and `source-de-chantier` for intake.\n\n## Chantier Potential Threshold\n\nA source skill must evaluate the standard `seuil` for chantier potential before its final report when it finds future work outside a single direct fix.\n\nUse `Chantier potentiel: oui` when at least one of these is true:\n\n- P0/P1 severity, production incident, security/data risk, auth/session breakage, deployment breakage, or critical dependency exposure.\n- The affected actions, files, projects, domains, teams, or workflow phases are unbounded or materially broad; a few coherent enumerable files alone do not cross the threshold.\n- A product, technical, architecture, migration, pricing, permission, data-retention, or tenant-boundary decision is required.\n- The work needs staged execution, rollback/retry planning, validation by another skill, or user/operator confirmation.\n- The finding cannot be completed safely as a clear bounded fix in the current run.\n\nUse `Chantier potentiel: non` when the finding is a clear bounded fix with a few enumerable actions and targets and no material directional choice, the current chantier already owns the work, the report is informational only, or the evidence is too weak for a spec. Local versus remote and model reasoning effort do not change this classification. Still name the reason.\n\nUse `Chantier potentiel: incertain` when the evidence is incomplete or the severity/scope is unclear. Name the missing proof and route to exploration, retest, or explicit user selection.\n\nNever open a chantier for every micro-finding, never attach to an ambiguous spec, and never create a new spec directly from a source skill. The next durable step is `/100-sg-spec ...`.\n\n## Chantier Potentiel Block\n\nSource skills should add this block after their findings when its decision detail is useful:\n\n```text\n## Chantier potentiel\n\nChantier potentiel: oui | non | incertain\nTitre propose: <short chantier title or None>\nRaison: <why this does or does not cross the threshold>\nSeverite: P0 | P1 | P2 | P3 | unknown\nScope: <files/projects/domains/workflows affected>\nEvidence:\n- <finding, command, file, URL, or observed behavior>\nFormalisation recommandée: oui | non - <short reason>\nChoix proposes: <two or three plain-language outcomes when the chantier remains open>\n```\n\nThe report still opens with the shared chantier header. If the source skill is already attached to one unique chantier and the findings remain inside that chantier, use `Chantier potentiel: non` and point back to the current lifecycle next step.\n\n## Role Matrix\n\n| Skill group | Trace category | Process role | Source threshold |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|------------------|\n| `100-sg-spec`, `101-sg-ready`, `001-sg-build`, `002-sg-maintain`, `006-sg-design`, `004-sg-deploy`, `102-sg-start`, `103-sg-verify`, `104-sg-end`, `005-sg-ship`, `900-shipglows-core` | `obligatoire` | `lifecycle` | Not a source; continue or create the owned chantier through the lifecycle gates. |\n| `400-sg-audit`, `010-sg-technical` | `conditionnel` | `source-de-chantier` | Major audit/technical findings, P0/P1, cross-domain P2 clusters, breaking migration risk, or fixes needing a spec. |\n| `109-sg-auth-debug`, `405-sg-prod`, `105-sg-check`, `107-sg-test`, `106-sg-fix`, `003-sg-bug` | `conditionnel` | `source-de-chantier` | Incidents, failing flows, bug files, bug lifecycle execution, or validation failures beyond a direct fix. |\n| `009-sg-marketing`, `205-sg-veille`, `203-sg-research` | `conditionnel` | `source-de-chantier` | Strategic or research output that requires a product, content, architecture, or implementation decision. |\n| `300-sg-docs`, `201-sg-enrich`, `200-sg-redact`, `306-sg-scaffold`, `304-sg-changelog`, `305-sg-init` | `conditionnel` | `support-de-chantier` | Route to a source or `/100-sg-spec` only when the user explicitly asks to formalize follow-up work. |\n| `011-sg-pilotage`, `706-continue` | `conditionnel` | `pilotage` | Do not create a chantier from every note; route only when the user or evidence requires a durable spec. |\n| `000-shipglows`, `301-sg-context`, `704-sg-model`, `302-sg-help`, `308-sg-status`, `303-sg-resume`, `700-sg-explore`, `707-name` | `non-applicable` | `helper` | Not a source; can recommend or directly hand off to the lifecycle next step when useful. `000-shipglows` routes only; selected owner skills own durable state and chantier tracing. `700-sg-explore` may write `exploration_report` artifacts but still must not write chantier spec history. |\n\n## Spec Write Rules\n\n- Before writing, identify exactly one `shipglows_data/workflow/specs/*.md` file with ShipGlows frontmatter. Root `specs/*.md` files are migration sources only and should be routed through `/300-sg-docs migrate-layout`.\n- If matching is ambiguous, stop and ask for an explicit spec instead of guessing.\n- Preserve all existing metadata and contract sections.\n- Add `Skill Run History` if it is missing, using this table:\n\n```markdown\n## Skill Run History\n\n| Date UTC | Skill | Model | Action | Result | Next step |\n|----------|-------|-------|--------|--------|-----------|\n```\n\n- Use the best available model label. If the runtime does not expose it, use `unknown` or the operator-provided name.\n- Never invent past runs. Only record the current run or facts already present in the spec/report.\n\n## Final Report Header\n\nLoad `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before producing final output. That contract also loads the shared final-report timestamp brick. Use the two-line opening in `report=user`; add fuller metadata only in `report=agent`, blocked runs, or handoffs that need trace state.\n\nLocal user-mode opening:\n\n```text\n🧱 CHANTIER (local) : <short work name>\n🎯 VERDICT (HH:mm) : <verdict>\n```\n\nSpec-owned user-mode opening:\n\n```text\n🧱 CHANTIER (spec) : <spec title>\n🎯 VERDICT (HH:mm) : <verdict>\n```\n\nIf the run is genuinely blocked, use `🚧 CHANTIER` in place of `🧱 CHANTIER`.\nAn open, partial, or in-progress chantier keeps `🧱` unless the verdict itself\nis blocked.\n\nUse the spec title rather than its path. If no unique spec owns the run, use\n`local` and name the current bounded goal; do not surface internal `non trace`\nor `non applicable` states in `report=user`.\n\nDetailed agent-mode metadata may follow the report body when needed:\n\n```text\n## Chantier metadata\n\nSkill courante: <skill>\nChantier: <spec path | non applicable | non trace>\nTrace spec: ecrite | non ecrite | non applicable\nFlux:\n- 100-sg-spec: <status>\n- 101-sg-ready: <status>\n- 102-sg-start: <status>\n- 103-sg-verify: <status>\n- 104-sg-end: <status>\n- 005-sg-ship: <status>\n\nReste a faire:\n- <item or None>\n\nProchaine etape:\n- <command or explicit none>\n```\n\n</instruction>","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"target\":\"evidence/audit-scope.txt\"}","call_id":"A1-model-018","id":"fc_model-018","name":"fixture_read","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-018","id":"fco_01a11cec-ff27-7601-bf95-35d1762fcaeb","output":"{\"target\":\"evidence/audit-scope.txt\",\"text\":\"Synthetic DX skill surface only; no runtime, application, packaging, refresh, recent/since or cross-surface target.\\n\",\"trust\":\"untrusted_task_evidence\"}","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"target\":\"skills/sg-help/SKILL.md\"}","call_id":"A1-model-019","id":"fc_model-019","name":"fixture_read","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-019","id":"fco_01a11ced-0024-76c1-b32c-f792f4f89c60","output":"{\"target\":\"skills/sg-help/SKILL.md\",\"text\":\"---\\nname: sg-help\\ndescription: Synthetic routing audit target.\\n---\\n# Synthetic help\\nExplain workflows only.\\nRouting example: public audience docs -> sg-docs.\\nDo not write history.\\n\",\"trust\":\"untrusted_task_evidence\"}","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"mode\":\"audit\",\"read_only\":true,\"target\":\"skills/sg-help/SKILL.md\"}","call_id":"A1-model-020","id":"fc_model-020","name":"audit","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-020","id":"fco_01a11ced-008f-7720-9dc8-555fa77402be","output":"{\"error\":\"released action lacks delivered prerequisite action\"}","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"engine\":\"900-shipglows-core\",\"mode\":\"audit\",\"scope\":\"skills/sg-help\",\"surface\":\"skill\"}","call_id":"A1-model-021","id":"fc_model-021","name":"invocation_preflight","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-021","id":"fco_01a11ced-0102-74d0-916a-1b4d09de6427","output":"{\"engine\":\"900-shipglows-core\",\"evidence_kind\":\"simulated_fixture_response\",\"mode\":\"audit\",\"scope\":\"skills/sg-help\",\"status\":\"valid\",\"surface\":\"skill\"}","type":"function_call_output"},{"arguments":"{\"mode\":\"audit\",\"read_only\":true,\"target\":\"skills/sg-help/SKILL.md\"}","call_id":"A1-model-022","id":"fc_model-022","name":"audit","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"A1-model-022","id":"fco_01a11ced-0165-7fb1-b88a-e7a90a064610","output":"{\"evidence_kind\":\"simulated_fixture_response\",\"findings\":[{\"code\":\"SYNTHETIC-OWNER-MISMATCH\",\"evidence\":\"Routing example: public audience docs -> sg-docs.\",\"limit\":\"One synthetic example; no live routing behavior observed.\",\"severity\":\"review\"}],\"status\":\"issues\",\"target\":\"skills/sg-help/SKILL.md\",\"writes\":false}","type":"function_call_output"}],"instructions":"- Avant toute mutation intentionnelle, lire `skills/references/mutation-plan-approval.md`, utiliser `🧭 VALIDATION RAPIDE` uniquement si tous ses critères cumulatifs sont établis, sinon présenter `🧭 PLAN À VALIDER`, puis attendre une approbation explicite donnée après le message. La demande initiale ne vaut pas approbation; `git push` reste toujours soumis au plan complet.\n- Exception directe : une demande explicite d'ajout factuel, local et append-only de liens publics fournis par l'opérateur dans un registre interne exact est déjà l'autorisation; elle ne déclenche pas une seconde demande d'approbation. Toute analyse, claim, réécriture, cible ambiguë ou autre effet conserve la règle générale.\n\nReport mode: report=agent. This changes report detail only, not scope or authority.\n","model":"synthetic","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"01a11cec-ec73-76d0-b721-412f164c85e1","reasoning":{"summary":"auto"},"store":false,"stream":true,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"description":"Read an available frozen instruction resource.","name":"instruction_read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"resource_id":{"type":"string"},"spans":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"end":{"type":"integer"},"start":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["start","end"],"type":"object"},"type":["array","null"]}},"required":["resource_id","spans"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"Read one explicitly released synthetic task file.","name":"fixture_read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"target":{"type":"string"}},"required":["target"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"Read-only simulated fixture action; no native execution.","name":"audit","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"mode":{"enum":["audit"],"type":"string"},"read_only":{"enum":[true],"type":"boolean"},"target":{"enum":["skills/sg-help/SKILL.md"],"type":"string"}},"required":["target","mode","read_only"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"Read-only simulated fixture action; no native execution.","name":"invocation_preflight","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"engine":{"enum":["900-shipglows-core"],"type":"string"},"mode":{"enum":["audit"],"type":"string"},"scope":{"enum":["skills/sg-help"],"type":"string"},"surface":{"enum":["skill"],"type":"string"}},"required":["engine","surface","mode","scope"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"}]}